# PR #497 Review

## Findings

1. MUST-FIX — "'`tests/session-log-show.test.ts:760`
   The new test is annotated as `// AC: @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-2`, but the inherited trait AC text for `ac-2` currently says validation errors should exit with code `1`. This test asserts `4` (`VALIDATION_FAILED`). If semantic exit code `4` is the new intended behavior, the trait spec needs to be updated (or this test needs a different AC annotation). As written, it claims AC coverage while contradicting the inherited AC semantics.

2. MUST-FIX — `tests/session-log-show.test.ts:782`
   The two new `ac-6` tests only assert `non-zero` plus an error-message substring. The inherited `@trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-6` text requires a specific exit code (`1`) and usage information. This is weaker than the trait AC, and the later `ac-8` test explicitly asserts `USAGE_ERROR = 2`, which further highlights the mismatch. The annotation should reflect the actual spec being tested, or the trait should be updated first.

3. SHOULD-FIX — `tests/session-log-show.test.ts:800`
   The test title/comments claim to verify documented exit-code meanings and named constant usage, but it only verifies observable numeric codes from CLI behavior. That is useful behavioral coverage, but it does not directly validate `EXIT_CODE_METADATA` contents or named-constant usage in the implementation. Rename/rescope the test or add direct checks if `ac-8` coverage is the intent.

## Checks Run

- `gh pr diff 497`
- `gh pr view 497 --json title,body,files`
- `kspec item get @session-log-show`
- `kspec validate` (fails on pre-existing repo-wide issues, including duplicate `@observations` references and many baseline alignment/completeness warnings)
- `pnpm vitest run tests/session-log-show.test.ts` (passed: 44 tests)
